  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "Slab placement, tilt and size, the fissure pattern and pebble hops vary per cast. The stomp time and the ring rhythm stay fixed so the hit lands at the same moment every cast."
  },
  "director_notes": "An original area quake around the caster (a genre move, nothing copied). Timing: a 0.45 s brace with a building rumble, faint trembling and a few hopping pebbles; a sharp stomp (impact + boom, dust pop, crater); then a rupture: fissures spread out in a full circle (decal fissures, reveal_ms) with a ring of dust, and an eruption layer with shape slabs heaves the ground up in four rings, slower (rise_ms 150) and longer-held than spikes so it reads as rolling ground, not attack spikes; an aftershock ring and pebbles bouncing over the whole area (sparks look rock with emit_radius_px) carry the long heave under a 6 Hz flickering shake; the slabs sink back and the cracks stay. Sound: rumble -> impact + boom -> crash -> long loud rumble -> quiet rumble. The caster is the centre (destination caster): every target standing in the circle is hit."
}
